Zero-X notices
==============

Zero-X house style (neuroncli/auth-server/src/house-style.js)
-------------------------------------------------------------
The short style preface that the Zero-X gateway adds to coding-agent requests
(docs.html#house-style, neuroncli/auth-server/docs/HOUSE_STYLE.md) is written in
Zero-X's own words. Its ideas were inspired by the public projects below, and
the wording was checked against the copies of their skill files that the Neuron
client bundles: no run of four words is shared with any of them
(neuroncli/auth-server/scripts/check-style-originality.mjs, a local script that
needs the Neuron client's bundled-skills directory). That check covers the
bundled copies only; it was not run against other versions of these projects.

- Ponytail, a rule set that makes a coding agent write the least code that
  works: https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail (original) and the fork
  https://github.com/dkfish/ponytail. MIT licence.
  Inspired the "Economy" section (is the change needed at all, does the
  platform, the language's library or the codebase already cover it) and the
  rule in "Build discipline" that shortening never removes input validation,
  data-loss handling, security or accessibility.
- gstack by Garry Tan, role-based workflows for planning, building, review and
  shipping: https://github.com/garrytan/gstack. MIT licence.
  Inspired the "Build discipline" habit of small, verified steps and running
  the tests. Its role-based pipeline is not part of the preface.
- anti-slop by miqdadbadjuber, a skill set against generic AI copy and UI:
  https://github.com/miqdadbadjuber/anti-slop, the version the Neuron client
  bundles (commit 388cbe3, recorded as MIT licence in the client's
  bundled-skills SOURCES.json). Inspired the "Design taste" section.
- Hallmark by Nutlope, an anti-slop UI design skill:
  https://github.com/Nutlope/hallmark. MIT licence according to its project
  page; we have not confirmed its LICENSE file or copyright line. Also
  inspired the "Design taste" section (choose a deliberate direction first,
  avoid default generic AI page patterns, real content, accessible layouts).

No text from these projects is copied or vendored here, so their licence
notices are not required for this code. If text from any of them is ever added
to the gateway, its licence file and copyright line must be added to this
notice in the same change. The Neuron client bundles the Ponytail, gstack and
anti-slop skills, with their licences, in its own repository.

The names above belong to their authors. Zero-X is not affiliated with them.
